# The front door's settings: an optional HTTPS front door (Caddy) for a machine that has none.
#
# For: whoever runs hq on a machine. Copy to `front-door/.env`; it is gitignored. Read by front-door/compose.yml.
# See docs/architecture/deployment.md.

# The domain for hq, e.g. hq.example.com; hq's HQ_URL must then be https:// + this.
HQ_DOMAIN=

# Optional: the host name uploaded files are served from, never hq's own (adr-0114),
# e.g. files.hq.example.com; hq's FILES_ORIGIN in hq/compose.env must then be
# https:// + this. Its DNS entry points at this machine too. Leave empty and hq
# offers uploads as downloads only.
FILES_DOMAIN=

# Optional: the preview domain, e.g. preview.example.com — the domain in
# PREVIEW_PATTERN in hq/compose.env (https://p-{id}.preview.example.com), which
# must be set too. Caddy needs the domain itself for its wildcard host name, not
# the pattern. Needs a wildcard DNS entry (*.preview.example.com
# pointing at this machine) and a wildcard certificate, which needs a DNS-provider
# challenge: a Caddy image with your DNS provider's plugin, and its API token below.
# See the Caddyfile. Leave empty to keep live previews off.
PREVIEW_DOMAIN=
DNS_API_TOKEN=
